Pipeline Map (Current)
 
Data Workflow and Process
1.	Step 6 runner builds the per-case payload.
2.	Runner calls build_sbom_context(matched_esn, til_profile_context).
3.	SBOM logic checks sbom_dependency_flag and strict part/MLI keys from profile context.
4.	SBOM logic tries Databricks SOT lookup first.
5.	If SOT rows are unavailable, logic falls back to local sample workbook parsing.
6.	Deterministic matching runs against normalized part and MLI values.
7.	sbom_context is returned with status, matches, condensed evidence, and notes.
8.	Final applicability prompt receives SBOM as supporting configuration evidence (not a hard gate).
Inputs and Contracts
Step 6 -> SBOM request shape
Key fields consumed from til_profile_context:
•	sbom_dependency_flag
•	sbom_trigger_reason
•	parts_referenced[].part_number
•	mli_numbers[].mli_number
Other key input:
•	matched_esn
Data sources used
Primary SOT sources:
•	vgpd.plm_hcd_std_views.plm_sbom_explosion_sot_vw
•	vgpd.plm_hcd_std_views.plm_sbom_deviation_details_sot_vw
Fallback source:
•	local sample SBOM workbook folder under context/data/source_examples/sbom
Matching logic (current)
•	deterministic normalization via normalize_cell
•	part matching supports exact normalized equality and 8-char prefix family behavior
•	MLI matching supports normalized variants through normalize_mli_variants
•	no embedding-based fuzzy retrieval in the current E6.3 path
Outputs
Returned context block includes:
•	status
•	source_type, source_file, source_tables
•	matched_esn, source_serial_numbers
•	strict_part_numbers, strict_mli_numbers
•	match_count, matched_sections
•	condensed_matches, raw_matches
•	notes
Status values seen in logic:
•	skipped_not_required
•	skipped_missing_strict_part_numbers
•	source_not_found
•	parse_error
•	no_match_found
•	matched
Key Methods and Responsibilities
From sbom_lookup.py:
•	extract_strict_part_numbers / extract_strict_mli_numbers: derive lookup keys from profile
•	load_sbom_sections_from_sot: query Databricks SOT SBOM rows
•	find_sample_workbook_for_esn + load_sbom_sections: local fallback parse
•	match_rows: deterministic matching across explosion/deviations sections
•	condense_matches: prompt-safe match compression
•	build_sbom_context: orchestrates request, source selection, matching, and output contract
Preliminary Experiment Findings
1.	SBOM logic is now integrated in active Step 6 payload assembly, not only in design notes.
2.	Databricks SOT-first with workbook fallback is implemented and resilient to missing-source cases.
3.	Matching is explainable and auditable because it is deterministic and row-preserving.
4.	Current design explicitly treats SBOM as supporting unit configuration evidence only.
5.	No-match does not imply not-applicable; it only means current SBOM source did not confirm the key.
Runtime and Production Gaps / Uncertainties
1.	Source coverage gap:
•	Some ESNs can fail both SOT and local fallback; production source SLAs are not yet formalized.
1.	Key quality gap:
•	SBOM lookup quality depends on profile extraction quality (part_number and MLI extraction completeness).
1.	Schema and join assumptions:
•	SOT column semantics and long-term stability should be validated with data owners.
1.	Signal calibration:
•	No documented confidence or strength weighting yet for different SBOM match types.
1.	Governance and observability:
•	Need explicit monitoring for SBOM source availability, parse errors, and match-rate drift.
Current Usage Guidance
Use E6.3 outputs as:
•	supporting structured evidence for applicability reasoning
•	a traceable context object for SME and CPM explainability
Do not use E6.3 outputs as:
•	hard exclusion logic when no matches are found
•	final applicability or completion verdicts
